    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented customerCode de-duplication so that distinct owners always receive distinct customer codes.\n\n**The rule:** when the computed `customerCode` already belongs to another owner, append `-<n>` using the smallest `n \u2265 2` that makes it unique; the owner is stored with (and returns) the de-duplicated code.\n\n**Changes, each kept in its proper unit:**\n\n1. **`CustomerCodeGenerator.deduplicate(baseCode, isTaken)`** \u2014 a pure, repository-agnostic method next to the existing `format`/`region` code. It takes a `Predicate<String>` for \"is this code taken?\" and returns the base code, or `base-2`, `base-3`, \u2026 \u2014 the smallest untaken suffix. Fully testable in isolation, no persistence knowledge.\n\n2. **`OwnerRepository.findByCustomerCodeStartingWith(prefix)`** \u2014 a new query that gathers the family of codes derived from one base (the base plus any `-<n>` variants). Implemented in all three impls that exist in the repo:\n   - `SpringDataOwnerRepository` (active `spring-data-jpa` profile) \u2014 derived query, no body needed.\n   - `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl` (`jpa` profile) \u2014 JPQL `LIKE`.\n   - `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl` (`jdbc` profile) \u2014 SQL `LIKE`, selecting `customer_code` so the code is populated.\n\n3. **`ClinicServiceImpl.assignCustomerCode(owner)`** \u2014 a small private helper that builds the base code (reusing the existing `LocalityResolver` + `CustomerCodeGenerator.format` logic), fetches the taken codes into a `Set`, and delegates to `deduplicate`. `createOwner` now just calls this helper instead of inlining the formatting, so no method grew into a catch-all.\n\nThe base code (`REGION-HASH8`) contains no SQL `LIKE` wildcards, so the prefix match is safe, and the `Set`-membership check makes the smallest-`n` search correct and O(1) per probe.",
